Subject: [PATCH] locale: timezone and languages come from the launch or host

The timezone and Accept-Language list are not drawn by seed. They come
from --fingerprint-timezone and --fingerprint-locale, which the Python
and Node packages fill from a GeoIP lookup of the exit IP, and otherwise
stay the host's own. A drawn zone guarantees a mismatch with the
connection's country, and a drawn language list disagrees with Intl
formatting a page can read in one call. The speech voice list follows
the named locale, so a launch without one keeps the host's voices.

