+// The note a named locale field carries.
+//
+// Deliberately not OverrideNote's: that one warns that a hand-picked value has
+// no prevalence data behind it and may be more distinctive than a drawn one,
+// which is true of a core count and false here twice over. There is no drawn
+// locale to be more distinctive than, and naming a zone that matches the
+// egress is the correct operation on this surface rather than a risk taken.
+// What the report does need to say is which of the two things that write this
+// switch wrote it, because a launcher's GeoIP answer and an operator's own
+// choice arrive identically and only one of them tracks the exit IP.
+std::string LocaleNote(std::string_view field) {
+  return "locale." + std::string(field) +
+         " was set from the command line: either named by the operator or "
+         "resolved by the launcher's prelaunch GeoIP lookup of the effective "
+         "egress. Neither the seed nor the catalogue reaches this surface";
+}
+
+// The note an inherited locale field carries.
+//
+// Says which switch would pin it, because the operator reading this report is
+// usually reading it to find out why a served value does not match an exit IP,
+// and "the host decided" plus "here is how to decide instead" is the whole
+// answer to that question.
+std::string LocaleInheritanceNote(std::string_view field,
+                                  std::string_view switch_name) {
+  return "no launch layer named locale." + std::string(field) +
+         ", so the host's own is served unchanged and nothing is composed for "
+         "it. On a direct egress that matches; behind a proxy it is the host's "
+         "and not the exit's. Pass " + std::string(switch_name) +
+         " to pin it, or launch through the Python or Node package, which "
+         "resolves it from GeoIP of the effective egress and passes that same "
+         "switch";
+}
